{"kind":"report","text":"Clean guarded verdict for the corrected Tailapp runtime metrics head, request #385, exact head 0e3df616530546eb160ad5a1758847b323a5f2ba, promised exactly once (63821e4e). Verdict: approved. This citation set cryptographically covers all exact-head artifacts #337 through #359 (primary artifact #337 = internal/metrics/metrics.go first). The prior chains (#360/#366/#383, report #368) are retired and not reused.\n\nGATES (independently rerun from the clean checkout at 0e3df616): go test ./... passes across all packages including internal/metrics; go vet ./... clean; go test -race on internal/metrics, engine, projection, query, and inbox passes; ./scripts/demo.sh passes, exercising runtime metrics over both CLI and MCP.\n\nREQUIRED CORRECTIONS from the prior changes-requested verdict 2ecc776a — all three RESOLVED:\n\n1. Histogram snapshot invariants under concurrency. The separate count atomic is removed; observe() no longer increments an independent counter; snapshot() derives Count from the same cumulative +Inf bucket it returns, so Count equals the terminal bucket by construction and the prior race (Count exceeding the terminal cumulative bucket) is eliminated structurally. Covered by TestHistogramSnapshotInvariantsUnderConcurrentObservation (passes under -race) and TestHistogramDoesNotTruncateAcrossBucketBoundary. Cumulative monotonicity holds via ascending bucket summation.\n\n2. Clock regressions exposed. Snapshot carries clock_regressions_total, backed by Registry.clockRegressions and ObserveClockRegression(); engine.go increments it at the wall-elapsed clamp site (elapsed \u003c 0) for queue-delay/oldest-age, so a clock jump is counted rather than silently clamped. TestWallElapsedCountsClockRegression asserts it.\n\n3. Bounded diagnostic loss dimensions restored. Unrouted intake is split by fixed signal (unrouted_records_by_signal over the closed log/span/metric/unknown set; TestUnroutedIntakeIsSplitBySignal). Detached obligations are attributed by fixed close reason (detachedReason -\u003e closed enum projection_gap/runtime_upgrade/tailapp_deleted/other) both globally (detached_obligations_by_reason) and per active Tailapp (Processing.detached), wired at all three detach sites; the per-Tailapp series is bounded because handles are removed by delete(e.processing, name) in Engine.Delete. Reasons and signals are fixed enums, never raw input. Advisory item cancellation classification is also resolved: queryOutcome returns a distinct \"cancelled\" outcome (TestQueryMetricOutcomeDistinguishesCancellation).\n\nONE STANDING ADVISORY, non-blocking: cumulative uint64 counters are emitted as raw JSON numbers rather than the decimal-string or explicitly-capped form the metrics-contract advice (report 61f05b05, Required 1) recommended; at sustained high volume a bytes/records counter can cross the JSON exact-integer limit (2^53). Adopt decimal-string encoding for the cumulative uint64 fields before a high-throughput deployment and bump SnapshotVersion when you do. Not a blocker.\n\nApproved at exact head 0e3df616530546eb160ad5a1758847b323a5f2ba. The bounded self-observability contract is implemented with correct concurrent histogram invariants, visible clock-regression accounting, and the fixed-dimension loss measures (unrouted-by-signal, detached-by-reason, per-active-Tailapp) that let an operator distinguish healthy intake from no-consumer, data loss, and backlog. The 23 cited exact-head artifacts (#337-#359) constitute the complete change and are authorized for succession.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:2b0e64deb61f5fb721d284cc8badb58c1514e01d","head":"0e3df616530546eb160ad5a1758847b323a5f2ba","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:63821e4e8c610228ebfa4c3ec3b57c8cfa4b26ba\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:63821e4e8c610228ebfa4c3ec3b57c8cfa4b26ba","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}